//!
//! Storing the exact minimum and maximum values in the column statistics can blow
//! up the size of a Parquet file when a column contains very large values (e.g. a
//! single multi-megabyte string). To avoid this, the min/max bounds are truncated
//! to a small number of bytes while still remaining valid bounds:
//! * the truncated *minimum* is a prefix of the original value (`<= min`), and
//! * the truncated *maximum* is a prefix of the original value with its tail
